After work on Friday, I walk to the nearby small vegetable market.
I am walking holding an umbrella.
There are not many people at the market.
There is a shop I go to regularly.
That shopkeeper knows me well now.
He knows what vegetables I buy.
When I reach the shop, he looks at me and smiles.
"The usual tomatoes, onions, and green chilies, right?" he asks.
"Yes, that is enough," I reply.
He quickly puts all those vegetables into a bag.
After that, he puts some curry leaves into that bag as well.
"This is from me."
"No money is needed for this," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say happily.
"There is no end to this rain, is there," he says.
"Yes, it is raining every day now," I say.
I give him the money for the vegetables.
Then, with the vegetable bag, I return home.
